# Frontend Rules Index

Entry point to Flutter technical standards for FCHIP (`frontend/`).

## Conflict order

When rules conflict, you must apply this order:

1. Security, privacy, and safety rules.
2. [`.cursor/app-write-up.mdc`](../../.cursor/app-write-up.mdc) for product identity and boundaries.
3. [`app-flows/`](../../app-flows/), then each screen's `app-ui/**/screen.json` and visual references.
4. [`backend/.cursor/api.mdc`](../../backend/.cursor/api.mdc) for HTTP and cross-stack behavior.
5. [`product_delivery.mdc`](./product_delivery.mdc), [`instant_ui_sync.mdc`](./instant_ui_sync.mdc), then [`realtime_sync.mdc`](./realtime_sync.mdc).
6. This index and the named owner file.
7. Other frontend rules, then `dev-plan/` steps for chronology.

## Invariants

- You must prioritize performance, uniform reusable UI in `frontend/lib/shared/`, real-time sync, full responsiveness, and simple workflows.
- Product implementation is frontend-first and paired: every UI screen ships with the backend that serves it, in the same atomic chronology unit (`S-NNN`), before the next screen starts. See [`.cursor/mandatories.mdc`](../../.cursor/mandatories.mdc) and [`slices/chronology.yaml`](../dev-plan/slices/chronology.yaml).
- Every screen must trace to `app-ui/<module>/<screen>/screen.json`; every journey must trace to `app-flows/`.
- Build order is `frontend/dev-plan/slices/chronology.yaml`; module slices (`VS-NN`) are ownership groups only.
- Entities must be referenced by `human_friendly_id` only; raw table IDs must not be exposed.
- Effective access must equal role/module/user grants ∩ subscription package ∩ assigned modules ∩ ABAC scope, defined in [`frontend/.cursor/permissions.mdc`](./permissions.mdc) and `backend/.cursor/auth-security.mdc`.

